# Titan Orbit — Windows late-join crash invariants

Relay late-join with hundreds of map ghosts hard-crashes the **Windows client**. Fixes keep getting undone by unrelated agents. **Do not regress these invariants.**

Paired: `titan-orbit-ship-simulation.mdc`, embedded NetCode (`Packages/com.unity.netcode`), `tools/netcode-patches/`.

---

## Root cause (proven in Player.log)

| Symptom | Cause |
|---------|--------|
| `Crash!!!` right after `[JoinSettle] TransformSystemGroup RE-ENABLED` | Disabling LTW during Instantiates of ~700 asteroids, then flipping the group back on → Burst LocalToWorld flood (2026-07-18 12:17) |
| `Crash!!!` right after `[TO_GhostSpawn] Created 56 placeholders` | CreateEntity×N in one frame with LTW on (2026-07-18 12:47). Also: distance TileSize 512 ≥ map size → whole field one chunk despite MaxSendChunks=1 |
| `Crash!!!` in `DrawAsteroids` / `MarkFromQuery` / `MinimapEcsEntitySync` → `ToEntityArray` | Gathering all asteroids — **including after settle** (2026-07-18 13:26 MarkFromQuery) |
| NRE in `TitanOrbitClientSafeLocalToWorldSystem` foreach | Full query over Instantiated bodies right after TransformSystemGroup RE-ENABLED |
| `baseline for a ghost we do not have` | Requeue leftovers without registering CreateEntity'd ghosts in `SpawnedGhostEntityMap` |

**Patterns that must never return:**
1. Disable → re-enable `TransformSystemGroup` / `LocalToWorldSystem` around join Instantiates.
2. CreateEntity dozens of placeholders in one frame (cap at 1 + requeue; keep Instantiates at 1).
3. Distance `TileSize` ≥ map size (must fragment asteroid fields).
4. Any `ToEntityArray` / `WithEntityAccess` over asteroids/planets/gems on the client join path — **settle ending does not make it safe**. Use baked Pending + small drains only.

**Silent crash?** No. `Crash!!!` is a native access violation in Burst/UnityPlayer. C# `try/catch` cannot swallow it. Only prevention (caps / gates) or process death.

